 "equipment_type": "Variable frequency drive (inverter)",
 "applies_to": "Mitsubishi Electric FR-E800 compact inverters with the built-in Ethernet port (FR-E8xx-E and safety/IP67 Ethernet variants) set to BACnet/IP.",
 "summary": "Ethernet versions of the FR-E800 serve a fixed BACnet/IP object set: two analog input terminals, monitor and command Analog Values (frequency, current, power, energy, PID, fault history, speed scale, PID commands, a parameter mailbox and accel/decel times), terminal state BIs and BOs, and status and command BVs (run/stop, direction, fault reset). Some terminal objects do nothing on certain model variants.",
 "bacnet_transport": [
  "BACnet IP"
 ],
 "firmware": null,
 "default_device_instance": 0,
 "access_inferred": false,
 "notes": [
  "Access codes as printed: R read-only, W read/write, C commandable (priority array).",
  "Footnoted BI/BO objects have no function on the Ethernet, safety-communication or IP67 models (see the manual's notes for each).",
  "Values written to commandable objects go to the priority array even when the inverter rejects them because of the operation mode.",
  "Speed scale and PID command objects are only applied when the speed command source is NET.",
  "Source: Section 2.8 BACnet/IP, 'Supported BACnet object', pdf pages 123-126."
 ],
